Third-party software in the APKs
================================

Mapsforge 0.23.0 (map rendering)
  https://github.com/mapsforge/mapsforge
  License: GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0 (LGPL-3.0)
  Jars: mapsforge-core, mapsforge-map, mapsforge-map-reader,
  mapsforge-map-android, mapsforge-themes (from Maven Central).
  The map theme's symbols and patterns (assets/symbols, assets/patterns) come
  from the mapsforge-themes jar and carry the licences stated there.
  android/car/assets/maptheme/quiet.xml is derived from Mapsforge's bundled
  default.xml render theme, and so is under the LGPL-3.0, not MIT.
  This repository holds the app's complete source and build scripts, so the
  APKs can be rebuilt against a modified Mapsforge.

BRouter 1.7.10 (offline routing)
  https://github.com/abrensch/brouter
  License: MIT. Copyright (c) the BRouter authors.
  Built from the release source by fetch.sh, which also copies the car-vario
  routing profile, lookups.dat and BRouter's LICENSE into assets/brouter.

ZXing core 3.3.3 (QR code reading, for joining a convoy)
  https://github.com/zxing/zxing
  License: Apache License 2.0. Copyright (c) the ZXing authors.

AndroidSVG 1.4 (SVG rendering)
  https://github.com/BigBadaboom/androidsvg
  License: Apache License 2.0. Copyright (c) Paul LeBeau, Cave Rock Software Ltd.

Root certificates (android/car/assets/certs)
  ISRG Root X1 and ISRG Root X2 (Internet Security Research Group, Let's
  Encrypt) and GTS Root R1 and GTS Root R4 (Google Trust Services LLC), as
  published by their certificate authorities. They let Android 4.4, whose own
  certificate store is out of date, make TLS connections to current servers.
  They are public certificates, included unmodified.


Map data
========

The maps (download.mapsforge.org) and routing tiles (brouter.de) the app reads
are made from OpenStreetMap data, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, under the
Open Database License (ODbL 1.0). They are not part of this repository.


Art, brand and voice
====================

The navigation voice pack (android/car/assets/voice/angie) was generated with
ElevenLabs text to speech. The built-in vehicle look (android/car/assets/profile)
was generated with an image model. Both are our
own work and are under the MIT License with the rest of this repository.
The profile's wordmark is set in Roboto (Apache License 2.0).

